toplevel-info: hold each toplevel handle's window weakly

LeandrOS port of the weak_window fix for the closed-window texture leak
(Smithay#1562, pop-os/cosmic-comp#2084), against cosmic-comp dec1ee86.

Every ZcosmicToplevelHandleV1 stored a strong clone of its window, and
remove_toplevel() never cleared it. The handle lives until its client
destroys it, so a closed window stayed reachable:
handle -> Window -> WlSurface -> data_map -> the last-buffer texture
(its GEM import, and on virgl its read_sync fence fd).

The handle now stores Window::Weak and upgrades it where it is used.
smithay efeb597 already has WeakWindow and cosmic-comp already has
WeakCosmicSurface, so smithay is not patched. toplevel_management
requests on a handle whose window is gone are ignored instead of
panicking on unwrap().

Upstream: cmeissl's diagnosis on Smithay#1562 (issuecomment-3864200389);
MartinKavik/cosmic-comp@weak_window_upstream_smithay.

